# No rules — deliberately. This file exists to record why there are none.
#
# The gallery is a client-routed single-page app, so a deep link such as
# /runs/<id> has no file behind it and must still be answered with the app shell
# and a 200. Cloudflare Pages does that on its own: a project with **no
# `404.html`** serves `/index.html` for an unmatched path, at the requested URL,
# with a 200. Deleting the old `404.html` is therefore the whole fix, and there is
# nothing left to configure.
#
# Do not add `/*  /index.html  200` here. Pages rejects it as an infinite loop —
# it strips `/index.html` back to `/`, which re-matches `/*` — and logs
# "Infinite loop detected in this rule and has been ignored" at build time. The
# rule does nothing except make the build look broken.
#
# What this replaced: a `public/404.html` that stashed the requested path in
# sessionStorage and bounced through `/` to restore it client-side. That is the
# GitHub Pages workaround, correct when the gallery was hosted there and carried
# over unnoticed when it moved to Cloudflare Pages. It cost a visible flash, and
# it served every run page to crawlers as an HTTP 404 with no markup — so a run
# link resolved to an error when shared and no run was indexable.
